Is maintenance in SWEBOK v4.0a limited to post-delivery, and was the cited ISO 14764 text inspected here?

Use these exact pinned knowledge graph excerpts and say what they do not prove:
{"claim":{"id":"se:CLM-07F-SWEBOK-MAINT-DEFINITION","statement":"SWEBOK Guide v4.0a defines software maintenance as the totality of activities required to provide cost-effective support for software in operation, performed in pre-delivery and post-delivery stages, and reports the ISO/IEC/IEEE 14764 objective of software maintenance as modifying existing software while preserving its integrity.","scope":"SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA7 Introduction and section 1.1; a professional-BOK definition citing ISO/IEC/IEEE 14764, whose text is metadata-only in this project.","limitations":"The ISO/IEC/IEEE 14764 objective is reported by SWEBOK; the ISO text was not independently inspected."},"evidence":{"id":"se:EVD-07F-SWEBOK-MAINT-DEFINITION","statement":"SWEBOK Guide v4.0a KA7 defines software maintenance as the totality of activities required to provide cost-effective support for software in operation, with activities performed during a pre-delivery stage (planning for post-delivery operations, maintainability, and logistics support for the transition from development to maintenance) and a post-delivery stage (software surveillance, modification, training, and operating or interfacing with a help desk). Citing ISO/IEC/IEEE 14764, it states the objective of software maintenance as modifying existing software while preserving its integrity, and notes the maintenance phase begins after a warranty or post-implementation support period while maintenance activities occur much earlier.","limitations":"The ISO/IEC/IEEE 14764 standard itself is registry metadata-only in this project; the objective is cited as SWEBOK reports it, not from the ISO text."},"locator":{"id":"se:LOC-07F-SWEBOK-KA7-MAINT-DEF","section":"SWEBOK Guide v4.0a, Chapter 7 Software Maintenance, chapter Introduction plus section 1.1 Definitions and Terminology; PDF page indices 166-167; printed pages 7-1 to 7-2"},"source":{"id":"se:SRC-SWEBOK-GUIDE-4-0A","title":"Guide to the Software Engineering Body of Knowledge (SWEBOK Guide), Version 4.0a","limitations":["A guide to the body of knowledge, not the complete body of knowledge","Generally accepted knowledge is not a uniform prescription for every project","Its topic citations are not comprehensive","Related disciplines are identified but not characterized in full"]}}
